    "encoding_note": "PCIe 5.0 uses the 128b/130b block encoding from Gen3: a 130-bit block = 2-bit sync header + 128 bits of scrambled payload. Modulation is two-level NRZ (PAM4 is Gen6). 8b/10b (Gen1/Gen2) is NOT used at Gen5."
